# session-`/clear` safety R2 — objective-tracker owner-pending lifecycle

Sub-amendment 1 of 3. Sealed local; awaiting dispatcher dogfood
publish per ASK-FIRST.

The objective-tracker gained an additive `ObjectiveStatus`
lifecycle value `owner_pending` — "work shipped, owner decision
pending" — distinct from `active` (in progress) and from the
terminal set `{achieved, abandoned}` (closed). This is the single
distinction a hand-maintained RESUME-STATE file existed to carry:
that a shipped item is awaiting the owner's call, not done. Added
`active→owner_pending` and `owner_pending→{active,achieved,
abandoned}` legal transitions plus the production runtime API
`ObjectiveTracker.mark_owner_pending`; no pre-R2 transition was
removed or altered (additive — amendment-38 widening precedent,
default-preserving, D8 round-trip). owner_pending is NOT terminal
and NOT default-in-flight: its own category so the session-start
digest never collapses it into "done" (R2.2 surfaces it in R1's
primary-persona digest fence per D-SCS.4). R2 is the hard input to
R1 — the priority-ordered digest cannot rank-by-owner-pending until
owner-pending is representable. AC.SCS-R2.{1,3,S} green against real
test output; full objective-tracker suite (incl. amendment-38
backward-compat + D8 round-trip) unchanged. SHA register +
method-decision record in the parent plan-doc §14.
